    {
      "id": "a3",
      "refs": ["w16"],
      "kind": "theology",
      "body": {
        "en": "*Liṅga* first means a mark, a sign. The Liṅga Purāṇa builds on that: Śiva Himself is *aliṅga*, without a mark, and from Him came the *liṅga*, the nature we can see, touch, taste, smell and hear, which it calls the body of the worlds. So the last two names meet: the moving and unmoving world is His form, and that world is His liṅga. The Śiva Purāṇa looks from the other side: the liṅga is His formless (*nirākāra*) sign.",
        "hi": "*लिङ्ग* का पहला अर्थ है चिह्न, निशान। लिङ्ग पुराण इसी से आगे बढ़ता है: शिव स्वयं *अलिङ्ग* हैं, बिना चिह्न के, और उन्हीं से *लिङ्ग* निकला, यानी वह प्रकृति जिसे हम देखते, छूते, चखते, सूँघते और सुनते हैं; पुराण इसे लोकों का शरीर कहता है। इसलिए अन्तिम दो नाम मिल जाते हैं: चर-अचर जगत् उनका रूप है, और वही जगत् उनका लिङ्ग है। शिव पुराण दूसरी ओर से देखता है: लिङ्ग उनका *निराकार* चिह्न है।"
      },
      "citations": [
        {"source": "mw-linga", "locator": "MW liṅga, p. 901,3", "quote": "a mark, spot, sign, token, badge, emblem, characteristic"},
        {"source": "linga-purana-1-3", "locator": "Liṅga Purāṇa 1.3.1", "quote": "aliṅgaḥ śiva ityukto"},
        {"source": "linga-purana-1-3", "locator": "Liṅga Purāṇa 1.3.3", "quote": "gandhavarṇarasairyuktaṃ  % śabdasparśādilakṣaṇam"},
        {"source": "linga-purana-1-3", "locator": "Liṅga Purāṇa 1.3.4", "quote": "vigraho jagatāṃ liṅgam  % aliṅgād abhavatsvayam"},
        {"source": "shiva-purana-vidyeshvara", "locator": "Śiva Purāṇa 1.5.11cd", "quote": "niṣkalatvānnirākāraṃ liṃgaṃ tasya samāgatam"},
        {"source": "mw-alinga", "locator": "MW a-liṅga, p. 95,1", "quote": "having no marks"},
        {"source": "mw-nirakara", "locator": "MW nir-ākāra, p. 540,1", "quote": "formless, shapeless, incorporeal"}
      ],
